  "section_notes": "S1 keeps mandatory incident reporting but limits the scope to confirmed incidents and only requires prompt customer notice. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% reporting threshold without automatic sales stop, while giving per-model results to buyers/regulators but not the public. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 36 months and retrofit to six years with a feasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notice and no transition."
